            "content": "Given these aspects:\n# Two Key Aspects of Vaccination\n\n1. **Individual Protection (Immunity)**\n   - Vaccines train the immune system to recognize and fight specific pathogens without causing the actual disease\n   - They provide personal protection by creating antibodies and immune memory cells\n\n2. **Community Protection (Herd Immunity)**\n   - When a high percentage of the population is vaccinated, disease spread is significantly reduced\n   - This protects vulnerable individuals who cannot be vaccinated (such as infants, immunocompromised people, or those with allergies to vaccine components)\nWrite one sentence connecting them."
          }
        ]
